from pathlib import Path
from PIL import Image,ImageDraw,ImageFont,ImageOps
import json,shutil,hashlib
ROOT=Path('C:/GrandTour');QA=ROOT/'Saved/LidarAuthoringQA/PaletteRefinement';CAP=QA/'Capture';OUT=ROOT/'Art/Export/LidarStudy/CohesiveStyle/PaletteReview';OUT.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True)
load=lambda p:json.loads(p.read_text(encoding='utf-8-sig'))
r=load(CAP/'process.json');assert r['ok'] and r['shader_validation_passed'];install=load(QA/'install.json');assert install['ok']
for p in CAP.glob('*.png'):shutil.copy2(p,OUT/p.name)
font=lambda n:ImageFont.truetype('C:/Windows/Fonts/segoeui.ttf',n)
for v in r['plan']['views']:
 ident=v['id'];board=Image.new('RGB',(1832,670),'#18201c');d=ImageDraw.Draw(board)
 d.text((20,12),'LIDAR / MOSS AND EARTH PALETTE',font=font(28),fill='#e5e2d3')
 d.text((20,53),v['title']+' / actual game frames, same camera and rendering settings',font=font(19),fill='#b9c2b2')
 for i,title in enumerate(['BEFORE / PREVIOUS PALETTE','AFTER / MUTED SHARED PALETTE']):
  x=20+i*906;d.text((x,96),title,font=font(20),fill='#e5e2d3');im=Image.open(OUT/(ident+('-before' if i==0 else '-after')+'.png')).convert('RGB');board.paste(ImageOps.contain(im,(886,500)),(x,136))
 board.save(OUT/(ident+'-comparison.jpg'),quality=95)

page='''<!doctype html><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width"><title>LiDAR palette refinement</title><style>body{margin:28px;background:#18201c;color:#e5e2d3;font:17px/1.6 system-ui}p{max-width:1100px}a{color:#bdccae}img{max-width:100%}.grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:20px}select{padding:10px}td,th{text-align:left;padding:10px;border-bottom:1px solid #536453}@media(max-width:800px){.grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}</style><h1>Moss, earth and muted sky</h1><p>The preferred broad-leaf meshes are restored. Their nearest LOD counts are back to 18,897 triangles for Mature/Edge and 5,945 for Pole. The rejected small-leaf experiment is retained separately, outside the active map.</p><p>The previous distance palette began at 40 metres, leaving close plants and ground in their brighter source colours. This pass adds a shared colour finish to nearby foliage, roads, clearings, sky and distance. Excess green shifts towards muted olive, saturation is restrained, and bright values receive a gentle roll-off. Dark shadows retain their value range. The distant forest, clearing, sky and haze colours are also adjusted to the same moss-and-earth family.</p><label>Compare <select id="view"><option value="valley">River valley</option><option value="road">Roadside materials</option><option value="leaves">Sunlit broad leaves</option></select></label><div class="grid"><div><h3>Previous palette</h3><img id="before" src="valley-before.png"></div><div><h3>Refined palette</h3><img id="after" src="valley-after.png"></div></div><p>Actual 888 × 500 game frames at 100% screen percentage. Each pair uses the same camera, exposure configuration and rendering settings in one run. Grass streaming can vary between captures. These images have not been colour-corrected outside the game.</p><h2>Per-map controls</h2><p>Open <code>LidarStudy_DistanceStyle → Profile → DA_Lidar_Evergreen</code>. Under <b>Palette Finish</b>, tune the controls below. The earlier palette is preserved as <code>DA_Lidar_BeforePalette</code>. Assign that profile for a complete visual rollback; setting Finish Strength to zero only disables the shared finish and retains the newly chosen distance colours.</p><table><tr><th>Control</th><th>Value</th><th>Purpose</th></tr><tr><td>Finish Strength</td><td>0.90</td><td>Amount of shared colour treatment.</td></tr><tr><td>Finish Saturation</td><td>0.80</td><td>Chroma across the composed view.</td></tr><tr><td>Green Restraint</td><td>0.80</td><td>Pulls excess green towards muted olive.</td></tr><tr><td>Highlight Compression</td><td>0.18</td><td>Restrains bright pasture, foliage and sky values.</td></tr><tr><td>Midtone Gain</td><td>0.92</td><td>Calms midtones while protecting low shadow values.</td></tr></table><p>Forest, Shadow, Sunlit, Clearing, Sky and Haze colours remain independent profile controls. Fog intensity/range, road parallax, planting, terrain and leaf materials were preserved.</p><p>The finish runs in the existing sky/haze material: no additional full-screen pass or texture sample. It adds shader arithmetic; GPU timings remain unverified while the GPU is shared.</p><p><a href="valley-comparison.jpg">Valley comparison board</a> / <a href="road-comparison.jpg">Road comparison board</a> / <a href="leaves-comparison.jpg">Leaf comparison board</a> / <a href="evidence.json">Validation evidence</a></p><script>document.getElementById('view').onchange=function(){for(let suffix of ['before','after'])document.getElementById(suffix).src=this.value+'-'+suffix+'.png'}</script>'''
(OUT/'index.html').write_text(page,encoding='utf-8')
e=dict(install=install,capture=r,leaf_restore=load(QA/'leaf-restore.json'),build='GrandTourEditor Development succeeded',performance_verified=False,sha256={p.name:hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest() for p in OUT.glob('*.png')})
(OUT/'evidence.json').write_text(json.dumps(e,indent=2));print(OUT)
